## 6. Data Retention and Deletion

Local game save data is retained on the user's device for the purpose of preserving game progress.

Users can delete locally stored Application data using the application management and storage options provided by the Android operating system.

Uninstalling the Application or clearing its application data through the Android device settings may permanently delete locally stored game save data.

Since HorozGame does not maintain an online user account system or server-side user save data, there is no online user account or server-side game data that must be separately deleted by the developer.

---

## 7. Data Security

Technology Store Simulator stores game save data locally on the user's device.

Because the Application does not transmit this save data to an external server, HorozGame does not maintain server-side copies of the user's local game saves and cannot remotely access them.

The security of locally stored data is subject to the security mechanisms provided by the Android operating system and the user's device.

Users are responsible for maintaining the security of their devices and preventing unauthorized access.

